<title>FRANCE: Danone confirms 1996 net at 3.38 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Danone confirms 1996 net at 3.38 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>French food group Danone confirmed in a statement its 1996 net attributable profit rose to 3.38 billion francs.</p>
<p>The company gave preliminary figures on January 29.</p>
<p>It gave the following final figures.</p>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable profit		  3,382  vs	   2,133</p>
<p>    Net attributable per share (francs)  46.33  vs	   30.96</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)		    17.00  vs	   16.00</p>
<p>    Operating income			   7,478  vs	   7,018</p>
<p>    Exceptional				  None   vs    loss 1,800</p>
<p>    Cashflow from operations		 7,951  vs	   7,424</p>
<p>    Free cash flow			     3,467  vs	   3,321</p>
<p>    Capital Expenditures		     4,484  vs	   4,103</p>
<p>    Turnover				    83,940  vs	  79,450</p>
<p>NOTE -- The company specified that its annual shareholders meeting will be held on May 14. Danone will pay the proposed 17 francs per share dividend only in cash from May 20, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
